From 5813eb2d57129c57a747e6c00767352a90948352 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:58:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Core: Holding.lent_workshops (workstream 09's patch 0001)
 [skip ci]

Workstream 09's patch 0001, applied as made to workstream 4's candidate
cf517b55: a Holding may take workshop copies out of its own continuous
arms production and lend them (rules: lend_workshops, reclaim_workshops,
own_arms; nothing changes while lent = 0, so no version or ruleset hash
moves), the reserve at 700 becomes LENT_WORKSHOPS (4 bytes, the same
layout otherwise), and the program, the verifier and the LiteSVM
harness read and write it; a capture clears it.

Tests (no key generation, derivation or signing): permutation-rules 513,
frontier-abi 146, permutation-frontier host 107 (108 with
custody-preview), workstream 09's kernel with core-patch-0001 44. The
verifier is built, not tested (its shared test helpers sign). SBF and
LiteSVM are not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2Y9wne2WBMdMysfzXe
